    "narrative": "For today\u2019s Independence Day slate, **Lawrence Butler** and **Tyler Freeman** anchor the offense, presenting as our most formidable options with scores of 74.61 and 72.83, respectively. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Sandy Alcantara, where a favorable park factor and strong platoon splits drive his elite rating. Meanwhile, **Tyler Freeman** finds himself in a prime position to capitalize on a shaky outing from Robbie Ray; the 18% boost from the opposing starter's skill profile, combined with the beneficial park dynamics, makes him a locked-in start. **Luis Arraez** also warrants mention, as the matchup against Sean Sullivan\u2014who holds an xERA of 6.43\u2014provides the perfect environment for his contact-heavy approach, pushing his efficiency score to an impressive 69.53.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 46.35 score. While **Gavin Sheets** offered value against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, the optimizer favored the higher ceiling and platoon advantages provided by **Daulton Varsho** and **Jonathan Aranda** in the final utility spots. We are closely monitoring the weather in the game featuring **Jeremiah Jackson**, as the 42% rain risk coupled with a tough matchup against Hunter Greene necessitates caution; if the game is delayed or pushed, **Jeremiah Jackson**\u2014currently sitting at a marginal 40.71\u2014will be the first to be swapped. We remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and the rest of the squad, as final confirmations will determine if our assumed batting orders hold, particularly for hitters like **Jung Hoo Lee**, who stands to gain significant value should he remain in the #5 spot against Sullivan.",
